Mechanism and acceptance evidence
- crates/bboxy450-harness-wake-up/src/capability.rs:73: O_EXCL/O_NOFOLLOW creation, exact 0600 descriptor permissions, 64 hexadecimal bytes plus newline. launch.rs:498 creates the file in the existing fresh 0700 launch overlay before any seat exec; launch.rs:593 and :625 pass the path through the Codex wrapper and env_vars.
- crates/bbt-supervisor/src/supervisor.rs:2408: remove inherited legacy admission before exec and ignore explicit legacy values. supervisor/companion.rs:52 removes it after service environment maps too. The isolated runtime removes legacy admission from inherited parent context.
- capability.rs:52, :98 and :136: shared regular-file/euid/mode/content validator, no-follow open, descriptor recheck and bounded 66-byte read; never unlinks on read. Typed Refusal codes are seat_admission_file_* so the existing secret scrubber preserves the reason without logging contents.
- crates/bbt-mux/src/mcp/bridge.rs:48 and adapters/hook.rs:67/:87 reopen on every start. Hook preflight precedes input parsing/OSC; failure stays quiet-success but is witnessed by its typed journal row, not exit status alone.
- crates/bboxy450-term/tests/capability_file.rs:61 proves shape, repeated reads, exclusive creation and refusal to overwrite a symlink target. :89 runs real bridge and hook processes for symlink, non-regular, wrong-owner, wrong-mode and malformed refusals: five reasons in each consumer. Wrong-owner uses metadata only for a foreign-owned file, or an owned chown fixture when privileged.
- capability_file.rs:170/:439 drives actual Supervisor, Logic, launch kit and app MCP/hook processes in an env-cleared private helper. Four initial kinds (claude, codex, zsh, bboxy450-harness), three generations per case: 12 cases, 36 child ps/env scans, zero capability-value copies, zero BBOXY_CAPABILITY= keys, 24 authenticated fresh MCP starts and 12 authenticated HookObserved replies. Scans stop at the owned supervisor, never the operator/real seat environment.
- capability_file.rs:459 onward checks distinct generation file paths and values, old path removal, refusal of copied old content by a new-generation endpoint after initialize, and final close removal. No raw value is printed.
- scripts/test-capability-control.py plus Makefile:1835 inject the actual value into the real exec path. Named assertion SeatAndAncestorEnvironmentIsCapabilityFree: red 101, restored green 0. Restored supervisor SHA256: ab9cd871db32e0073b4d0a6de38f0559fd38854977b296becc261fa26339bc37.
- Makefile:799 includes these fixtures in test-harness-native, followed by the real installed Codex direct and cold/forwarding-shim witnesses. Both resume after seat restart, preserve the borrowed daemon after seat/app close, make zero external model calls and require zero operator input.
- .bboxy/interfaces/app-harness.md:19-30 updates #348's crossing, startup, lifetime and verification rows for Oracle signature under d4071. No Side B/core harness files were changed.
- formal_contracts/capability_models.rs and verification inventories define separate environment/cleanup good-control pairs. Bounds are three fresh births, idle/live/stopping, current file birth and old-file/value markers; publish, repeated reads, stop and reap are atomic. No fairness/liveness claim is made. OS permissions, exclusive/no-follow creation, parser limits, real ancestry and authentication are implementation witnesses, not arbitrary Rust refinement.

